    "id": "l1_m4_h3_nu0_nonzero_b_tangent_exclusion",
    "title": "L1 m=4, h=3, nu=0 nonzero-b tangent exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For nu=0 and nonzero depressed constant b, every tangent root lies on H=kappa with kappa=-48 alpha a^2/Delta, while the tangent radical has degree at least 5-deg H. This excludes deg H=1,2; at deg H=0 it forces H=kappa and R(0)Delta+12a^2g(R(0))=0, and at deg H=3 there are only two or three tangent roots. The b=0 arm and endpoint cases remain open, so L1 is not closed.",
